  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>lillietest</keyword>
  <short_description>Lilliefors goodness-of-fit test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>h = lillietest(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = lillietest(x, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p] = lillietest(...)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p, kstat, critval] = lillietest(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>lillietest</b> performs a two-sided Lilliefors goodness-of-fit test with parameters estimated from the sample. <b>NaN</b> observations are omitted.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Distribution</b>, and <b>MCTol</b>. Supported distributions are normal, exponential, and extreme value. <b>MCTol</b> is accepted for syntax compatibility; this implementation uses a deterministic approximation.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [-1 -0.5 0 0.5 1];
[h, p, kstat, critval] = lillietest(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
